<title>USA: General Motors unit sells $500 mln notes.</title>
<headline>General Motors unit sells $500 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from General Motors Acceptance Corp, the finance arm of General Motors Corp, was priced Monday, according to lead manager Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p>BORROWER GENERAL MOTORS ACCEPTANCE CORP</p>
<p>AMT $500 MLN	 COUPON 7.125 PCT  MATURITY 5/1/2001</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.681  FIRST PAY DATE 11/1/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A3    YIELD 7.218 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD +40 BP     CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>NOTE: PRICED AT 40 BASIS POINTS OVER THE 6-1/2 PERCENT U.S.</p>
<p>TREASURY NOTE DUE MAY 2001.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
